## SQ-CBB-01 | chain: removed recipe count back to normal, no refused remove from pack scripts
@group A (chain)
@commands boot; `shell grep -h "Added [0-9]* recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log`
@pass removed count under 500 (r1106cba: 3823 with the bad filter, 312 without); `bootreject remove refused: filter\.output.*dish_stuffed`
@fails a `remove refused` line names the next undefined key: fix that script's key (the guard works)
@from batches/r1106cbb/c1.qb passed
shell grep -h "Added [0-9]* recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log
shell n=$(grep -oE "removed [0-9]+ recipes" logs/kubejs/server.log | tail -1 | grep -oE "[0-9]+"); echo "removed=$n"; test "$n" -lt 500
bootreject remove refused: filter\.output.*dish_stuffed
shell grep -h "remove refused" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/kubejs/startup.log | head -20

## SQ-CBB-02 | NCH remove guard probe
@group A (chain)
@commands copy `tools/scratch_query/nch_guard_probe.js` to `srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_nch_guard_probe.js` before the boot; `kjsexpect \[nchguard\] normal remove of minecraft:bread done`; `shell grep -c "remove refused" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/kubejs/startup.log`
@pass 4 `remove refused` lines from the probe (paths `filter.output`, `filter.input`, `filter.not[0].id`, `filter`), every case logs `case done`; `> cdevtest recipes minecraft:bread` lists no `minecraft:bread` id
@fails `NCH.remove` / `_undefinedIn` in neoCraftHelper.js; a Java Ingredient walked as an object (prototype check)
@from batches/r1106cbb/c1.qb passed
@reviewed 2026-11-16
kjsexpect \[nchguard\] normal remove of minecraft:bread done
shell grep -h "\[nchguard\] case done" logs/kubejs/server.log | sed 's/.*\] //'
shell test "$(grep -h "\[nchguard\] case done" logs/kubejs/server.log | wc -l)" = 4
shell grep -h "remove refused" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/kubejs/startup.log | sed 's/.*remove refused/remove refused/'
shell test "$(grep -h "remove refused" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/kubejs/startup.log | wc -l)" = 4
> cdevtest recipes minecraft:bread
sleep 2
reject verb=recipes id=minecraft:bread result=
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

## SQ-CBB-03 | fermenting count, Pale Jane and Steel Toe, bark and metal dust tags in Common
@group A (chain)
@commands `> cdevtest bytype brewinandchewin:fermenting`; `> cdevtest recipes creativebrewing:fermenting/pale_jane`; `> cdevtest recipes creativebrewing:fermenting/steel_toe`; `> cdevtest tag item immersive_weathering:bark`; `> cdevtest tag item creativeengineering:bark`; `> cdevtest tag item creativeengineering:metal_dusts`; `bootreject Couldn't load tag\|missing references`
@pass fermenting 18 or more (21 minus kombucha, kippers until CBB-05 is settled, and steel toe stout while `metal_dusts` has no chain member); `pale_jane_from_rice_wine` listed; `immersive_weathering:bark` empty and `creativeengineering:bark` holds `farmersdelight:tree_bark`; `metal_dusts` exists (0 members on the chain unless the owner added one)
@fails the tag move into Common (sweep list in the run doc section 2)
@from batches/r1106cbb/c1.qb passed
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest bytype brewinandchewin:fermenting
> cdevtest recipes creativebrewing:fermenting/pale_jane
> cdevtest recipes creativebrewing:fermenting/steel_toe
> cdevtest tag item immersive_weathering:bark
# judge-3, 2026-11-18: the tags are creativecommon: since 2026-11-09 (ids follow the owning jar); creativecommon:bark is
# #immersive_weathering:bark only (no farmersdelight:tree_bark any more), so the row checks that both tags exist
> cdevtest tag item creativecommon:bark
> cdevtest tag item creativecommon:metal_dusts
sleep 3
expect verb=bytype serializer=brewinandchewin:fermenting n=(1[89]|[2-9]\d)$
expect pale_jane_from_rice_wine
expect verb=tag kind=item tag=creativecommon:bark n=
expect verb=tag kind=item tag=creativecommon:metal_dusts n=
bootreject Couldn't load tag .*(creative|brewinandchewin|vinery)|missing references.*(creative|brewinandchewin|vinery)
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

